00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:33.220
First question comes from Jeremy.

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:38.460
Jeremy is a young entrepreneur, 20 years old,

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:43.460
and he has just a little bit of advice about his time

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:47.840
because he currently is working full-time

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:50.380
in a collections office,

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:54.300
but his real dream is to start a clothing business,

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.460
a clothing line.

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:56.520
Okay.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:58.560
But what happens is he works so hard

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:00.300
when he goes to his day job

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:03.280
that when he gets home, he's exhausted

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:07.360
and he's just not sure what he should do

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:09.880
because he's not finding that he has time

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:12.240
to actually work on his passion,

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:13.660
which is his clothing line.

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:19.780
So my, thanks for the question, Jeremy.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:24.760
I think feeling like you have a lack of time

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:28.500
is definitely common amongst anyone

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:32.820
who wants to pursue their dream.

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:36.460
And I think that the first thing

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:38.660
is to look at your situation,

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:42.840
and the good news is that you have a job,

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:46.460
that you have the ability to be making money

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:51.300
because maybe right now that's teaching you skills

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:54.420
that you may need for your business,

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:56.520
but also being able to make money

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:59.400
that you could be thinking about saving

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:02.480
to invest into this clothing line.

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:03.540
That's the good news.

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:06.880
You know, your job could be a means

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:09.760
to getting to this clothing line.

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:13.240
But I think the biggest,

00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:16.000
it can kind of be an excuse that we tell ourselves

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:19.360
that we don't have enough time

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:22.360
because at the end of the day,

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:24.980
you have limited time,

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:27.900
but I believe that we all have limited time

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:29.740
and we all have to learn how to use

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:32.900
the limited time that we have.

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:37.200
So to make it really practical for you,

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:38.420
I'd be asking yourself,

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:41.180
what's something you can do daily

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:46.320
that is a non-negotiable time

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:49.360
that you could spend every day on your business?

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:53.780
And I think even it might feel like

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:54.940
you're not getting a lot done,

00:03:54.940 --> 00:03:59.660
even if it's that 30 minutes right after you eat dinner,

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:01.540
you know, before you go to bed

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:03.860
to get up and grind the next day,

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:08.060
that 30 minutes just committing to it non-negotiable,

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:13.660
and that little amount can lead to good results

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:15.980
if you're consistent with it.

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:20.980
So I think it's kind of a lie that we don't have enough time.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:25.520
I think there's always a way to make time for what you love.

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:31.920
What do you think, sir?

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:32.740
Yeah, over to me.

00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:33.580
All right, cool.

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:35.720
Yeah, a couple things.

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:40.720
One, in agreeing with Rishy, you never had the time.

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:45.020
It's like, when is the right time to have a baby?

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:46.400
Well, there's never the right time,

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:48.520
but you have to look after that baby, right?

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:50.760
And when it's crying at three in the morning,

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:52.800
you gotta get up and look after that baby.

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:56.800
And so your business is your baby too,

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:58.800
and you're not looking after it,

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:01.560
and you need to make the time to be able to look after it,

00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:04.360
whether it is like, I'd like the half an hour a day idea,

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:08.160
whether that's at a certain time,

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:09.840
like whether you wake up half an hour earlier,

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:12.760
or whether you're staying up half an hour late,

00:05:12.780 --> 00:05:15.420
whatever it is, to make sure that there's progress.

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:16.460
The other thing I would say though,

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:18.420
is I would try to find a job where I'm learning

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:21.460
about the industry that I wanna get into,

00:05:23.020 --> 00:05:25.700
because you can learn so much by doing it yourself,

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:28.140
and hustling, and researching,

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:30.800
and that half an hour a day you'll learn,

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:33.460
but you'll learn a lot more when you're being mentored,

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:35.420
and when you can spend a lot more time on it.

00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:39.300
And so if your job was in collections,

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:40.220
is that what it was?

00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:42.260
Jeremy's job was in collections?

00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:43.480
Exactly.

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:44.320
Right.

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:46.440
So he's not learning much about the clothing business

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:49.040
by being in collections, apart from I guess,

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:51.680
how to make people pay when they don't pay you.

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:54.640
There's some kind of skill to learn there,

00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:59.560
but otherwise, yeah, you're not gonna be making money,

00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:00.880
you're not gonna be learning about

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:03.360
how to make money in that industry.

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:06.600
So what I'd suggest is go find a job in the business

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:10.240
where you can learn, not in some huge company,

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:12.780
but in a smaller company where you can learn

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:14.380
from the CEO founder.

00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:15.580
I usually like to look for companies

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:17.940
that are about 10 employees or less,

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:21.180
someone who's established, but not yet so big

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:23.700
that your job will just be fetching coffee

00:06:23.700 --> 00:06:25.940
and really mean your work.

00:06:25.940 --> 00:06:28.060
And get to know them, and learn from them,

00:06:28.060 --> 00:06:30.700
and be inspired by them, and take on more projects,

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:33.140
and volunteer to be involved more often

00:06:33.140 --> 00:06:35.180
in the things that they're doing.

00:06:35.180 --> 00:06:37.780
Because you'll learn about the industry,

00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:39.540
and you'll learn to make connections,

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:44.200
and you'll make mistakes while getting paid to do it,

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:46.680
instead of making all those mistakes on your own.

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:50.560
And so the reason to get a job is to learn.

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:54.240
And so if you're having a hard time

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:57.040
in your collections industry and trying to figure out

00:06:57.040 --> 00:06:58.840
how to make more time for your business

00:06:58.840 --> 00:07:01.500
and pursue your passion, then yes,

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:04.320
I agree with setting half an hour a day,

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:06.780
even if you're exhausted, to go and work it.

00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:09.920
But then also, I'd be looking at switching my job

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:13.320
so that I'm learning, because that's gonna really

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:16.140
multiply your efforts and get you there a lot faster.

00:07:19.240 --> 00:07:20.080
Nice.

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:23.160
Now Evan, sorry, really quickly,

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:25.160
we've got some people wanting to watch the stream

00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:26.520
and they're not seeing you live.

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:30.080
I'm not seeing you live, but I thought it was just on my end.

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:32.360
Yeah, I saw that too, I don't know.

00:07:32.360 --> 00:07:34.400
It says I'm streaming and it's recording,

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:36.000
so at least we'll be able to upload it to YouTube.

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:38.740
I don't know what's going on with Twitch today.

00:07:38.740 --> 00:07:40.340
Gotcha, okay.

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:46.680
Yeah, a job in working with another fashion designer

00:07:47.380 --> 00:07:50.420
sounds a lot more exciting than working in collections.

00:07:51.620 --> 00:07:54.380
For him, right?

00:07:54.380 --> 00:07:55.220
Yeah.

00:07:55.220 --> 00:07:56.580
A person who wants to start a collection business

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:59.120
should learn about the collections industry first.

00:08:00.920 --> 00:08:02.800
So if you're not learning from your job,

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:05.300
for any of you who are watching who have a job

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:08.160
and you're not liking it, as soon as you stop learning

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:10.480
at your job, it's time to move on.

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:12.400
It doesn't mean you have to start your own business yet,

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:13.900
you may not be ready, you may not have the financial

00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:15.640
resources, you may not have the knowledge, experience,

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:17.960
be able to provide the value, all that stuff,

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:20.440
but if you're not learning at your job anymore,

00:08:20.440 --> 00:08:21.960
then you're just wasting time.

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:24.280
You gotta go do something that at least you're learning

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:27.760
new things about, and that meaning you bounce

00:08:27.760 --> 00:08:30.020
from a couple jobs until you find the one

00:08:30.020 --> 00:08:32.520
that you're really learning, makes you come alive.

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:37.200
Great, hope that helps you Jeremy.

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:38.040
Good luck.

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:40.760
Good luck.

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:43.240
Next question comes from Nathan.

00:08:43.240 --> 00:08:46.240
Nathan says, he's at the very beginning stages

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:49.960
of being an entrepreneur, he's looking for a job,

00:08:51.320 --> 00:08:54.320
and so it kind of sounds like he's in the same situation

00:08:54.320 --> 00:08:56.880
a little bit with Jeremy, trying to get a job

00:08:56.880 --> 00:09:01.880
that will give him some skills in his ultimate dream

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:03.840
of being an entrepreneur.

00:09:03.840 --> 00:09:08.220
He says he thought that telemarketing would be a good fit

00:09:08.220 --> 00:09:13.180
for him when he was thinking about some of his strengths,

00:09:13.180 --> 00:09:18.180
but later he felt like the telemarketing jobs were,

00:09:21.020 --> 00:09:24.020
in his own words, going to kill his character.

00:09:24.020 --> 00:09:29.020
He thought it may be a little dishonest, stressful,

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:34.520
so he's wanting just general advice about what he should do

00:09:37.320 --> 00:09:41.440
as he looks for a job as an aspiring entrepreneur.

00:09:43.320 --> 00:09:48.320
Okay, so Nathan, I think, I definitely don't think

00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:54.640
that all telemarketing jobs necessarily require

00:09:54.640 --> 00:09:57.360
that you have to be dishonest or that

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:01.360
I think the main thing about telemarketing jobs

00:10:01.360 --> 00:10:06.360
is finding a company and a product that you actually feel

00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:11.980
you believe in and that will give value to your customers,

00:10:11.980 --> 00:10:16.040
because obviously you do have to be someone

00:10:16.040 --> 00:10:19.760
who's going to successfully sell that product,

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:23.600
and so the way to not feel dishonest

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:25.520
is to actually be selling something you think

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:27.640
will really help people, and I think that would take away

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:29.620
a lot of the feelings of dishonesty.

00:10:32.420 --> 00:10:35.220
So it sounds like your strengths are maybe,

00:10:36.100 --> 00:10:38.380
you're maybe you're interested in sales,

00:10:39.220 --> 00:10:44.220
maybe the dealing with people, interpersonal skills

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:47.300
was something that was attractive to you about that,

00:10:47.300 --> 00:10:48.700
so if it's something that you think

00:10:48.700 --> 00:10:50.820
you still really want to pursue,

00:10:50.820 --> 00:10:54.980
I would say try to find a company and a product

00:10:54.980 --> 00:10:57.420
that you actually really believe in,

00:10:58.240 --> 00:11:00.640
and I think that will take care of the feeling

00:11:00.640 --> 00:11:02.280
that it would kill your character.

00:11:03.360 --> 00:11:06.640
Aside from that, though, I want to know more

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:11.640
about your actual business, because I then would be able

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:14.000
to give you a little bit better feedback

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:16.680
in regards to maybe some alternatives.

00:11:16.680 --> 00:11:19.560
I mean, telemarketing may not be the best fit.

00:11:19.560 --> 00:11:22.320
I know for me in general, like if I'm looking for jobs,

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:27.820
I definitely want to be in a place that is going

00:11:29.820 --> 00:11:34.100
to bring out my strengths or help me

00:11:34.100 --> 00:11:36.180
make my strengths even stronger.

00:11:37.580 --> 00:11:40.840
So maybe telemarketing isn't actually the best fit,

00:11:40.840 --> 00:11:42.540
but maybe there are other ways

00:11:42.540 --> 00:11:44.100
that you can be involved in sales,

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:47.340
or being involved with dealing with learning

00:11:47.340 --> 00:11:49.260
how to communicate with customers

00:11:49.720 --> 00:11:54.000
that will then give you some of the skills

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:56.400
that you want to bring to your business later on.

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:00.960
I like it.

00:12:00.960 --> 00:12:01.880
Yeah, what are you passionate about?

00:12:01.880 --> 00:12:03.200
What are you passionate about, Nathan?

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:06.760
I'd love to hear more about what really gets you excited.

00:12:10.400 --> 00:12:11.240
What do you think, Evan?

00:12:11.240 --> 00:12:12.080
I like it.

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:15.120
I got my Timo jungle on, so it's a good start.

00:12:15.120 --> 00:12:16.760
Yeah. It's a good start.

00:12:16.760 --> 00:12:18.400
Yes.

00:12:18.860 --> 00:12:19.760
This was Nathan?

00:12:21.620 --> 00:12:22.460
This is Nathan.

00:12:22.460 --> 00:12:23.280
Nathan.

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:26.140
Yeah, so one, I guess, for everybody writing,

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:28.580
I was going to say Colin, everybody writing in,

00:12:28.580 --> 00:12:31.060
yeah, a little bit more context helps

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:33.200
when you're presenting a challenge

00:12:33.200 --> 00:12:34.620
to know the situation a little bit more.

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:38.220
It doesn't mean you have to write 10-page long life story,

00:12:38.220 --> 00:12:39.820
because that usually gets ignored,

00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:43.780
but what kind of business do you want to start

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:45.780
would be pretty helpful.

00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:48.340
I'm assuming that you want to get into telemarketing

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:49.960
because you want to learn how to sell,

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:52.400
because in whatever business you're going to get into,

00:12:52.400 --> 00:12:54.200
you're going to have to learn how to sell.

00:12:54.200 --> 00:12:56.660
I would say, unless you want to start

00:12:56.660 --> 00:12:58.600
a telemarketing company,

00:12:58.600 --> 00:13:01.440
don't go work at a telemarketing company.

00:13:02.560 --> 00:13:05.400
Similar to Jeremy, the last one,

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:11.040
I would say look at a company that has 10 employees or less

00:13:11.040 --> 00:13:12.740
in the industry that you want to start.

00:13:12.740 --> 00:13:15.560
If you wanted to start in the fashion business,

00:13:15.580 --> 00:13:19.860
you might say, well, I want to learn how to sell,

00:13:19.860 --> 00:13:21.860
so I'm going to get a telemarketing job,

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:23.820
and that's going to teach me the skills,

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:25.620
and then I can move on.

00:13:25.620 --> 00:13:28.140
What I love about Nathan's approach is that

00:13:28.140 --> 00:13:30.420
he's trying to get a job where he can learn

00:13:30.420 --> 00:13:31.780
so that he can start the business,

00:13:31.780 --> 00:13:33.940
so it's not just earning a paycheck,

00:13:33.940 --> 00:13:35.880
but he's going to learn something that will help him.

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:38.740
The thing is, if you want to learn how to sell clothes,

00:13:38.740 --> 00:13:41.140
it may not be the best start

00:13:41.140 --> 00:13:43.100
to go to a telemarketing company.

00:13:43.100 --> 00:13:47.620
If you are going to go work, intern, volunteer, whatever,

00:13:47.620 --> 00:13:51.200
at a fashion company right now,

00:13:51.200 --> 00:13:52.640
they're going to sell.

00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:54.880
How do they sell their stuff right now,

00:13:54.880 --> 00:13:58.120
and how can you be on the sales team and learn from them?

